# ProofLens — Vercel project settings / local .env
# VITE_* values are public build-time configuration. Private keys are
# server-only and must never use a VITE_ prefix.

# --- GenLayer V2 ---
# NO GENLAYER PRIVATE KEY IS USED OR ACCEPTED BY THIS APP.
#
# The live v5 contract (0x01498130561f8629EdfDf4Edc881BEa3999E1C35) is pinned
# as the default in src/lib/config.ts and api/_lib/env.ts.
# -> All on-chain READS (get_report, get_report_count, get_latest_report_id)
#    work with NO credentials at all.
# -> On-chain WRITES are signed by the USER's own GenLayer wallet (MetaMask +
#    GenLayer Snap) in the browser. The user pays their own gas.
# -> There is no server signing route. Users sign in MetaMask themselves.
#
# The contract address is intentionally not configurable via env. This avoids
# stale deployment settings silently sending users to an old contract.

# --- Optional account history ---
# Contract submission no longer depends on PostgreSQL.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# --- Optional overrides ---
# PGSSLMODE="disable"                                  # only for local postgres without TLS

# --- Email sign-in (only saves scan history; wallets stay off) ---
# PROVIDER A · Privy hosted email authentication.
# dashboard.privy.io → create app → Login methods: EMAIL ONLY → disable
# embedded wallets. The browser needs only the public App ID; server-side
# token verification uses Privy's public JWKS endpoint, so NO app secret
# is ever required here.
VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID=""
# PRIVY_APP_ID=""            # optional server copy (functions read either)

# PROVIDER B · self-hosted fallback (used when VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID is absent;
# runs the built-in /api/auth OTP). Without RESEND_API_KEY it runs in dev
# mode and returns the code in the API response — fully testable locally.
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
# AUTH_EMAIL_FROM="ProofLens <login@your-domain.xyz>"  # default: onboarding@resend.dev

# --- Session signing secret (self-hosted provider only) ---
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32. Without it a deterministic development
# secret is derived from DATABASE_URL.
# SESSION_SECRET=""
